WEBVTT

00:00.430 --> 00:04.190
<b>We return to the Agency's office</b>

00:05.190 --> 00:06.430
It's...

00:06.430 --> 00:08.260
The Agency office!

00:08.640 --> 00:09.970
But how?

00:09.970 --> 00:11.990
I can't blame you for being shocked.

00:09.980 --> 00:11.990
<b>Ideals</b>

00:13.170 --> 00:14.490
Kunikida-san.

00:14.490 --> 00:16.660
But didn't the military police...

00:16.660 --> 00:18.330
Look outside the window.

00:22.030 --> 00:23.440
Isn't this...

00:23.440 --> 00:25.140
Tanizaki and Kenji are back.

00:25.140 --> 00:26.420
We have all our chess pieces.

00:26.780 --> 00:30.800
We had Poe-kun make a novel dimension
for us so we could hold a meeting.

00:30.800 --> 00:32.260
A meeting?

00:32.260 --> 00:33.540
You know what it's about.

00:33.540 --> 00:36.360
We're going to fight the enemy and win.

00:37.020 --> 00:40.450
This is the meeting for our final mission 
to save the Detective Agency.

02:11.020 --> 02:14.260
We hereby convene the
 Detective Agency general meeting.

02:14.700 --> 02:17.190
First, we'll review our situation.

02:17.190 --> 02:17.770
Rampo.

02:18.130 --> 02:20.900
Our enemy's plan is in its final phase.

02:21.680 --> 02:24.320
They've spread the vampire 
contagion throughout the world.

02:24.650 --> 02:27.440
Sixteen national militaries 
have already fallen.

02:28.200 --> 02:31.780
The armies, having become 
vampires, are eerily silent.

02:31.780 --> 02:33.090
For now, at least.

02:33.420 --> 02:35.870
What are these "vampires" 
you're talking about?

02:36.180 --> 02:38.290
The result of the immortal
 Count Bram's special ability.

02:38.800 --> 02:43.340
He turns those he bites into 
vampires over whom he has control.

02:43.830 --> 02:47.770
Those who are bitten can then
 further spread the contagion.

02:48.180 --> 02:49.150
In other words...

02:49.450 --> 02:52.470
The enemy grows exponentially.

02:52.760 --> 02:57.540
Bram is a pillar of the ten tragedies 
that once destroyed humanity.

02:57.990 --> 03:01.860
He was defeated by hero Fukuchi Ouchi 
and imprisoned with a holy sword.

03:02.360 --> 03:05.900
But that, too, must have been
 a mere step in his plan.

03:06.260 --> 03:09.150
The vampires have no trouble 
sneaking into organizations.

03:09.870 --> 03:13.060
The armies can't tell who's 
a vampire and who isn't,

03:13.060 --> 03:16.170
which is already causing 
them to turn on each other.

03:16.170 --> 03:20.610
Is it the enemy's goal to 
cause chaos around the world?

03:20.980 --> 03:23.300
No, that wouldn't work.

03:23.660 --> 03:28.810
The tyrant of Europe, the master of 
Gifted warfare, is still waiting.

03:29.510 --> 03:33.340
If they were to fight, based on sheer numbers,
 peace would be restored in six months or so.

03:33.340 --> 03:35.290
Then what's the enemy's objective?

03:36.420 --> 03:38.560
The enemy's true goal is

03:39.520 --> 03:40.820
The One Order.

03:41.600 --> 03:44.080
One of the three great calamities 
that was sealed away.

03:44.320 --> 03:48.910
<b>South Pole
British-French
 Joint Military Base</b>

03:44.390 --> 03:48.920
A wretched special ability weapon 
of mind control, born of the war.

03:51.660 --> 03:56.420
<b>Extreme
 Environment
Special Ability
Safekeeping Subject
Terminal</b>

03:56.740 --> 04:01.010
<i>Special governmental confinement designation 
electrocardiographic authentication confirmed.</i>

04:04.890 --> 04:09.500
<i>Special governmental confinement designation 
biometric authentication confirmed.</i>

04:12.120 --> 04:14.490
I'm retrieving the artifact 
designated for confinement.

04:14.490 --> 04:15.420
Authorize.

04:15.830 --> 04:20.080
<i>Special governmental confinement designation 
voiceprint authentication confirmed.</i>

04:30.630 --> 04:33.280
<i>Removing protective flammable fluid.</i>

04:33.280 --> 04:35.970
<i>Removing protective corrosive fluid.</i>

04:35.970 --> 04:39.960
<i>In accordance with Article 18 of 
the Standard Island Agreement,</i>

04:41.570 --> 04:45.840
<i>you are authorized to retrieve confinement 
designation subject One Order.</i>

04:49.250 --> 04:51.310
What is the One Order?

04:52.130 --> 04:54.320
How many bullets on average 
do you think it takes

04:54.330 --> 04:56.930
for a soldier to kill an 
enemy on the battlefield?

04:57.400 --> 05:00.160
Somewhere between five 
to ten to take out one?

05:00.160 --> 05:03.720
Including cover fire and suppressive fire, 
maybe a whole magazine or more.

05:04.490 --> 05:07.000
I'd guess it takes thirty to sixty bullets.

05:07.400 --> 05:08.610
No...

05:08.610 --> 05:10.110
It has to be more than that.

05:10.870 --> 05:11.730
Fifty thousand.

05:13.030 --> 05:15.990
Most soldiers don't even fire 
in the enemy's direction.

05:16.480 --> 05:19.180
They aim elsewhere,
only pretending to fight.

05:19.570 --> 05:24.660
Even in combat, people cannot tolerate
 the thought of killing another with a gun.

05:24.960 --> 05:26.430
That is the soldier.

05:26.800 --> 05:28.450
That is the war zone.

05:30.130 --> 05:33.440
Neither you nor Fukuzawa 
know that battlefield.

05:33.740 --> 05:37.540
That's why you can believe 
in a benevolent state.

05:38.340 --> 05:41.570
That's why the One Order was developed.

05:41.570 --> 05:43.850
I'll take it from here.

05:44.570 --> 05:47.560
The One Order is a weapon with 
an ability that is similar to mine.

05:48.320 --> 05:50.330
It affects its subordinates.

05:50.970 --> 05:56.590
It is a transmitter that ensures that 
subordinates follow all orders.

05:57.930 --> 06:01.830
When a commander uses this transmitter, 
developed by a Gifted engineer,

06:02.200 --> 06:05.850
a subordinate moves as though they 
are part of the commander's body,

06:05.850 --> 06:08.120
carrying out orders autonomously.

06:08.820 --> 06:11.300
They do not question,
and they do not feel guilt.

06:12.040 --> 06:15.330
The weapon frees a soldier 
from the shackles of crime.

06:15.330 --> 06:17.270
A merciful weapon.

06:19.770 --> 06:21.600
So it was supposed to be.

06:22.290 --> 06:24.690
I'm sure you can see where this is going.

06:25.090 --> 06:28.620
This transmitter was so dangerous 
that it was designated for confinement.

06:29.180 --> 06:30.650
Do you know why?

06:32.640 --> 06:34.160
A military coup.

06:34.690 --> 06:37.890
If a supreme commander 
were to use the One Order,

06:37.890 --> 06:41.550
they could take control of an entire 
military and overthrow the government.

06:42.030 --> 06:45.760
Having realized that possibility, 
the government sealed it away.

06:45.760 --> 06:46.900
Sealed...

06:47.380 --> 06:49.880
In other words, it wasn't <i>destroyed</i>.

06:50.110 --> 06:51.520
It ought to have been.

06:52.140 --> 06:55.320
They must have considered the possibility of 
a global crisis like the one we're in now.

06:55.900 --> 06:57.840
That, in itself, was good foresight.

06:58.380 --> 07:03.050
But what do you think will happen 
if Fukuchi uses the One Order?

07:03.050 --> 07:04.100
I see!

07:04.100 --> 07:05.510
This is a disaster!

07:06.270 --> 07:10.310
Fukuchi's men will take all the 
world's forces under his command.

07:11.000 --> 07:12.290
The Army of Mankind.

07:12.790 --> 07:14.810
If Fukuchi uses the One Order,

07:14.810 --> 07:18.280
humanity will become a single entity with
 the capacity to fight against the vampires.

07:18.960 --> 07:21.250
All according to Fukuchi's script.

07:21.620 --> 07:27.200
In other words, the Decay of Angels' 
goal is as cliché and stale as it gets:

07:29.010 --> 07:30.570
world domination.

07:33.120 --> 07:36.860
Twelve hours from now, 
Fukuchi will receive the One Order.

07:36.860 --> 07:39.660
If we can stop him, we win.

07:40.310 --> 07:43.030
I'll explain my plan to make that happen.

07:43.800 --> 07:46.310
He'll be retrieving the One Order...

07:46.320 --> 07:49.320
<b></b>Episode 55

07:46.320 --> 07:49.320
<b>At the Port 
in the Sky 
(Part 1)</b>

07:46.710 --> 07:47.920
At the airport.

07:52.790 --> 07:55.270
Seriously, Dad, you deadbeat!

07:55.600 --> 07:57.480
If he forgets something
 at the airport again,

07:57.480 --> 08:00.090
I'm gonna put a toothpick 
in his somen noodles.

08:00.600 --> 08:02.170
Um...

08:02.170 --> 08:04.720
Where's the lost and found?

08:04.720 --> 08:07.420
<i>The suspect is thought to be a member 
of the Armed Detective Agency.</i>

08:08.240 --> 08:10.060
<i>Assistant Senior Attorney Tonan 
has announced</i>

08:10.060 --> 08:13.840
<i>that the role of the terrorist organization 
known as the Armed Detective Agency</i>

08:13.840 --> 08:16.800
<i>will be officially recognized in the ongoing 
disappearances of military personnel overseas.</i>

08:18.640 --> 08:19.960
I told you...

08:21.060 --> 08:24.430
I won't let you kill anyone on my watch.

08:24.860 --> 08:25.790
Didn't I?

08:27.170 --> 08:29.550
<i>There's no way you're a terrorist.</i>

08:29.550 --> 08:32.630
<i>So why are they saying that on TV?</i>

08:32.630 --> 08:33.400
Out of my way.

08:37.270 --> 08:38.750
Hey, you!

08:40.090 --> 08:41.370
<i>That uniform...</i>

08:41.370 --> 08:42.480
<i>Are they police officers?</i>

08:42.880 --> 08:44.530
I'm here.

08:44.970 --> 08:49.040
So, are you sure the Detective Agency
 is going to show up here?

08:49.040 --> 08:50.290
<i>The Detective Agency?!</i>

08:50.290 --> 08:53.040
Are you questioning your captain?!

08:53.040 --> 08:54.340
Do you dare commit treason?!

08:54.340 --> 08:55.400
Of course not.

08:55.400 --> 08:57.050
I'm just skeptical.

08:57.380 --> 08:59.910
There are 18 decoy operations

08:59.910 --> 09:03.800
being executed in parallel to 
transport the One Order to Japan.

09:04.150 --> 09:06.650
Are you sure mere Detective Agency 
members could know

09:06.650 --> 09:09.060
that the real shipment is 
coming to this airport?

09:09.600 --> 09:12.550
The captain said they would,

09:12.550 --> 09:15.690
that the brat would no doubt figure it out.

09:15.960 --> 09:18.170
In that case, we have a problem.

09:18.170 --> 09:20.170
Are we going to fight in this airport?

09:20.610 --> 09:24.620
We may as well threaten their 
relatives and associates.

09:25.530 --> 09:27.330
Well, well.

09:27.330 --> 09:28.550
Judging from your heartbeat,

09:28.550 --> 09:32.090
you must be a relative or an associate 
of a Detective Agency member.

09:32.090 --> 09:33.800
So what if I am?

09:33.800 --> 09:35.890
I haven't done anything wrong!

09:35.890 --> 09:38.550
It's irrelevant who you are.

09:38.860 --> 09:40.960
If I were to hoist you above a fire,

09:40.960 --> 09:44.780
the Detective Agency would come to your 
rescue fully knowing that it would be futile.

09:44.780 --> 09:45.810
Am I mistaken?

09:46.200 --> 09:49.850
And you're going to set up someone 
who's kind enough to come rescue me?

09:50.490 --> 09:56.140
I don't care whether the
 Detective Agency is villainous or not.

09:56.480 --> 10:00.990
I simply want to hurt 
people and torment people

10:00.990 --> 10:03.630
and hear the sounds of their demise, 
under the rule of law.

10:03.630 --> 10:04.590
This is crazy!

10:04.590 --> 10:06.560
How is someone like you a police officer?!

10:06.560 --> 10:09.580
If you're defending the Agency, 
you're a suspect, too.

10:10.620 --> 10:14.790
Would you like to be a
 part of my entertainment?

10:15.550 --> 10:17.120
I wouldn't...

10:18.160 --> 10:18.950
Yeowch!

10:18.950 --> 10:20.320
That's enough.

10:20.320 --> 10:22.380
Do not use the innocent 
for your own amusement.

10:22.380 --> 10:24.540
Stop jabbing me in the ass!

10:24.540 --> 10:28.850
I'm just asking a suspect 
for their cooperation!

10:28.850 --> 10:32.060
Then do it after filing for 
a criminal negotiation.

10:32.060 --> 10:33.810
Otherwise it isn't justice.

10:34.250 --> 10:36.820
Why don't we settle this now, then?

10:37.110 --> 10:39.290
Let's see whose methods are right.

10:43.230 --> 10:44.340
Stop!

10:46.080 --> 10:47.630
Captain!

10:52.230 --> 10:53.710
I apologize.

10:53.710 --> 10:55.800
I'm here to protect your smiles.

11:01.010 --> 11:03.640
Do you really have time to be fighting?

11:04.040 --> 11:06.760
Today is literally the decisive battle.

11:07.200 --> 11:08.640
I apologize.

11:09.290 --> 11:12.130
The operation commences at 1200.

11:12.130 --> 11:14.970
Make sure we have enough encryption keys.

11:15.670 --> 11:16.410
Jouno.

11:16.410 --> 11:17.060
Sir.

11:18.040 --> 11:19.600
I want to show you something.

11:20.010 --> 11:21.270
Come with me.

11:22.450 --> 11:24.860
What do you think of the 
Detective Agency's tactics?

11:25.200 --> 11:27.380
They're highly skilled.

11:27.380 --> 11:30.820
Deploying coin bombs,
using vampires to take over armies...

11:31.280 --> 11:34.680
So long as the economy is what it 
is and the state is what it is,

11:34.680 --> 11:36.000
there's no stopping them.

11:36.000 --> 11:38.250
They seem to share my tastes.

11:38.870 --> 11:42.970
To be honest, I sympathize with 
their torturous tendencies.

11:43.690 --> 11:47.320
So, what is it that you wanted to show me?

11:48.800 --> 11:49.810
Captain?

11:49.810 --> 11:53.270
This is what I wanted to show you.

11:55.370 --> 11:58.430
Bram-kun, how far have you gotten 
into taking over the airport?

11:58.430 --> 12:02.460
I've already turned nearly half of 
the security force into vampires.

12:02.460 --> 12:03.510
What?!

12:03.510 --> 12:08.740
Remember Tachihara screaming about how there's 
a mastermind who set up the Detective Agency?

12:09.980 --> 12:12.000
I'm that mastermind.

12:13.630 --> 12:14.760
Jouno...

12:15.500 --> 12:18.380
Are you interested in 
helping me with my work?

12:26.570 --> 12:29.470
They don't seem to be aware 
of the location of this room.

12:29.770 --> 12:31.470
Let's go over our plan.

12:32.060 --> 12:33.980
Twenty-five minutes from now,

12:33.980 --> 12:38.560
a European escort team will arrive with the 
One Order on a camouflaged passenger plane.

12:38.950 --> 12:42.980
We'll intercept it and destroy it
 before it reaches Fukuchi.

12:43.360 --> 12:47.480
With the One Order lost, their plan 
will be delayed by at least two weeks.

12:47.990 --> 12:51.320
That'll be enough time for the 
Special Operations Division

12:51.320 --> 12:54.030
to expose Fukuchi's scheme to 
governments around the world.

12:54.460 --> 12:58.730
In other words, we'll have won without 
having to fight Fukuchi at all.

12:58.730 --> 13:01.970
But won't the enemy be trying to stop us?

13:01.970 --> 13:03.540
Exactly.

13:04.070 --> 13:06.340
And we're going to use that against them.

13:12.850 --> 13:13.750
Jouno.

13:14.240 --> 13:16.730
You're an oddity even 
among the Hunting Dogs.

13:17.060 --> 13:22.330
You place no trust in the squad, 
only thinking of them as a vessel.

13:22.330 --> 13:23.700
You're a lost dog.

13:23.700 --> 13:27.050
You have what it takes to become a 
member of the Decay of Angels.

13:27.050 --> 13:28.240
Say what?

13:28.240 --> 13:33.290
I hear you forced a band of 
bank robbers to kill themselves.

13:34.140 --> 13:35.710
Let's play a game.

13:37.170 --> 13:39.330
Stab yourselves in the gut with that sword.

13:39.330 --> 13:42.930
Anyone who gets the tip to pierce 
through their back will be free to go.

13:43.840 --> 13:46.890
I push this through my stomach and out my back?

13:46.890 --> 13:51.060
Isn't that preferable to 
being arrested and executed?

14:02.180 --> 14:04.200
Thank you for the fantastic sound.

14:07.360 --> 14:15.460
Jouno, you were a member of a 
criminal organization when I took you in.

14:15.990 --> 14:18.160
All for this day.

14:20.930 --> 14:21.850
And?

14:22.310 --> 14:24.980
What would you have me do?

14:24.980 --> 14:28.090
I want you to assassinate the 
Detective Agency members.

14:29.400 --> 14:31.840
The plan to take the One Order...

14:32.150 --> 14:34.440
Has one critical weakness.

14:34.860 --> 14:36.210
A weakness?

14:36.210 --> 14:39.780
There's actually a far easier target 
to destroy than the One Order.

14:40.740 --> 14:42.470
We just need to kill Bram.

14:43.060 --> 14:48.270
Bram needs to be brought along in order 
to give new orders to the vampires.

14:48.580 --> 14:52.780
But unlike the One Order, 
Bram won't be escorted by the Hunting Dogs.

14:53.070 --> 14:56.500
Therefore, as we're preventing 
the transfer of the One Order,

14:56.820 --> 14:59.580
we'll make it our true 
objective to eliminate Bram.

15:00.380 --> 15:03.750
That's surely the
 Detective Agency's plan about now.

15:03.750 --> 15:08.200
They'd never imagine that Bram would be 
protected by the Hunting Dogs, as well.

15:08.460 --> 15:12.850
Are you offering to let me enjoy the 
sound of the Agency's panic and despair?

15:12.850 --> 15:13.930
That's right.

15:15.990 --> 15:17.610
All right.

15:17.610 --> 15:20.510
I'll accept my mission as a
 member of the Decay of Angels.

15:20.750 --> 15:22.250
You're sure?

15:22.250 --> 15:26.530
You said you hired me for this 
very purpose. How could I refuse?

15:28.340 --> 15:29.340
Good.

15:29.780 --> 15:32.780
I've already decided where 
we'll attack the Detective Agency.

15:32.780 --> 15:33.620
Come.

15:38.120 --> 15:42.920
You should never have committed robbery if 
you weren't prepared to stab your own stomach.

15:45.590 --> 15:47.680
Thank you.

15:47.680 --> 15:50.890
I thought I was going to die 
after we were taken hostage.

15:51.670 --> 15:58.100
I will never forget what 
you've done for me, officer.

16:07.940 --> 16:09.730
Why, Jouno?!

16:09.730 --> 16:12.550
This was your own doing, Captain.

16:13.000 --> 16:19.330
You made the mistake of teaching 
me the joy of protecting someone.

16:19.330 --> 16:23.540
Compared to that, the sound of a 
pained howl is no better than silence.

16:23.880 --> 16:25.340
I see.

16:25.340 --> 16:27.420
You, too, betray me?

16:27.670 --> 16:31.170
<b>Amenogozen</b>

16:28.100 --> 16:30.640
Ritual sword Amenogozen!

16:49.430 --> 16:51.670
I'm disappointed, Jouno.

16:51.670 --> 16:54.490
But if you are another trial for me...

16:54.490 --> 16:56.130
I need only overcome!

17:03.290 --> 17:04.800
<i>Jouno's ability...</i>

17:04.800 --> 17:06.160
<i>Disintegration.</i>

17:06.160 --> 17:10.130
I'll be reporting the events that took place 
here to the vice captain and to Tetchou-san.

17:10.540 --> 17:15.130
With so much evidence, my testimony 
ought to be enough to convince them.

17:15.440 --> 17:17.130
You're done.

17:17.550 --> 17:19.640
Goodbye, Captain.

17:24.660 --> 17:25.950
<i>What is this?</i>

17:26.340 --> 17:28.430
<i>I can't get through the 
space between the door frame!</i>

17:28.440 --> 17:31.190
<b>Space Fracture</b>

17:29.680 --> 17:31.190
Space fracture.

17:34.800 --> 17:38.710
To think I'd be betrayed by my 
own and saved by a vampire...

17:39.390 --> 17:41.190
Now, Jouno...

17:41.570 --> 17:43.230
Are you prepared?

17:43.530 --> 17:44.880
<i>Be strong...</i>

17:44.880 --> 17:46.170
<i>There's nothing to worry about.</i>

17:46.440 --> 17:49.410
<i>The Amenogozen is strong, 
but it's ineffective on particles.</i>

17:49.740 --> 17:53.760
<i>If I can't get through the door, I'll simply 
escape through the air conditioning vent.</i>

17:54.620 --> 17:55.390
What the...?!

17:55.610 --> 17:56.450
Jouno.

17:56.850 --> 17:58.370
You're strong.

17:58.880 --> 18:05.360
Did you really think I wouldn't have come 
prepared before I revealed my true plans to you?

18:05.360 --> 18:07.110
Sword of flames!

18:07.110 --> 18:09.410
And it's fueled by the 
captain's favorite liquor!

18:09.410 --> 18:13.090
Your ability allows you to become 
minute particles of dust.

18:13.090 --> 18:17.620
And the best way to deal with dust 
is to gather it and set it on fire!

18:19.750 --> 18:23.230
If he burns away any more of my particles, 
I won't be able to return to human form.

18:23.230 --> 18:26.340
I'll have to undo my special 
ability and let him cut me

18:26.340 --> 18:29.590
so that I can blunt the fire 
with my blood and escape!

18:36.140 --> 18:40.180
I stabbed you with my sword 
from multiple futures.

18:44.030 --> 18:45.920
It's over, Jouno.

18:45.920 --> 18:49.310
You're right. It seems 
that it's over for me.

18:49.310 --> 18:51.230
But you...

18:52.220 --> 18:59.380
You aren't even aware of the 
suffering that is certain to befall you.

19:00.020 --> 19:02.390
And that is so pleasant for me.

19:05.000 --> 19:09.190
You're true to yourself even 
in your final moment, Jouno.

19:09.190 --> 19:10.340
Take him.

19:17.200 --> 19:18.520
<i>Captain...</i>

19:18.520 --> 19:20.830
<i>There's something you're wrong about.</i>

19:21.050 --> 19:25.560
<b>I didn't become aware of your conspiracy today.</b>

19:21.350 --> 19:25.550
<i>I didn't become aware 
of your conspiracy today.</i>

19:25.860 --> 19:30.000
<i>The heartbeat I heard from
 Tachihara-kun that day betrayed a lie.</i>

19:31.010 --> 19:34.220
<i>But it wasn't enough to be certain.</i>

19:34.640 --> 19:39.600
<i>So, just to be safe, I set up an 
insurance policy before I came here.</i>

19:41.740 --> 19:43.900
<i>What was that about?!</i>

19:43.900 --> 19:45.610
<i>A vampire leader?!</i>

19:45.950 --> 19:48.630
<i>I just read this note...</i>

19:48.950 --> 19:54.990
I don't care whether the 
Detective Agency is villainous or not.

19:55.000 --> 20:01.720
<i>Believer of the Detective Agency's innocence, 
follow me discreetly so as not to be detected.</i>

19:55.520 --> 20:01.710
<i>Believer of the Detective Agency's innocence, 
follow me discreetly so as not to be detected.</i>

20:02.370 --> 20:06.090
<i>I didn't get a good look, 
but an officer cut down another...</i>

20:06.090 --> 20:07.940
<i>And one of them...</i>

20:08.660 --> 20:10.690
I'm that mastermind.

20:11.550 --> 20:14.130
<i>So the Detective Agency 
was innocent all along.</i>

20:14.130 --> 20:17.880
<i>And yet they're being treated 
like criminals by everyone.</i>

20:18.660 --> 20:21.650
<i>I'm going to expose what
 I just heard to the world.</i>

20:22.000 --> 20:24.840
<i>That'll clear the 
Detective Agency's name, too.</i>

20:24.840 --> 20:26.940
<i>I believe in justice!</i>

20:27.720 --> 20:29.150
<i>Right, a picture!</i>

20:31.220 --> 20:34.920
<i>That'll prove he's in cahoots 
with that casket guy.</i>

20:36.540 --> 20:38.250
<i>Shoot! The flash!</i>

20:41.740 --> 20:43.710
<i>One of Jouno's people?</i>

20:44.230 --> 20:45.960
<i>I don't care who it was.</i>

20:46.250 --> 20:50.300
<i>Anyone who's taking pictures 
in here is doubtless an enemy.</i>

20:50.710 --> 20:51.630
<i>Do I run?</i>

20:51.630 --> 20:52.190
<i>I can't!</i>

20:52.490 --> 20:53.930
<i>There's no exit in this room!</i>

21:08.460 --> 21:10.040
<i>That was close.</i>

21:10.400 --> 21:12.950
<i>I would have been dead 
if I'd hid over there.</i>

21:13.240 --> 21:17.460
<i>I left the room right as 
he broke the window...</i>

21:17.840 --> 21:20.280
<i>But this is where my luck runs out.</i>

21:20.280 --> 21:21.750
<i>He's definitely going to hear me</i>

21:21.750 --> 21:25.230
<i>when I open the door to the hallway, 
and that's the only way out.</i>

21:35.660 --> 21:36.500
<i>Oh, no!</i>

21:36.500 --> 21:37.640
<i>He's coming back!</i>

21:37.960 --> 21:39.600
<i>Do I hide in the closet?</i>

21:39.920 --> 21:40.900
<i>I can't!</i>

21:40.900 --> 21:42.860
<i>He'll just cut down the entire hiding spot!</i>

21:42.860 --> 21:44.440
<i>What do I do?</i>

21:49.620 --> 21:50.880
<i>Wait...</i>

21:50.880 --> 21:53.320
<i>I think I could hide there.</i>

22:06.740 --> 22:07.980
No one's here.

22:09.040 --> 22:10.370
Impossible.

22:10.370 --> 22:12.150
Where are you hiding?

23:35.970 --> 23:39.970
<i>At the Port in the Sky (Part 2)</i>

23:35.970 --> 23:39.990
Episode 56
